            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0294" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">504.418A2/248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Diekema</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-04-07T16:00:00-05:00">April 7, 1930—4
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>25. For Miller. Your 46, Conference No. 13.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d203-f1"/> We
                    think you should refuse to sign convention and make statement to the effect
                    indicated by you. We do not think you should sign with reservations. Proposed
                    Articles 1 and 2 seem to us more objectionable even than you indicate.</p>
                <p>Your 17.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d203-f2"/> We think it better to say at the
                    conference that your delegation has recommended against signature and you do not
                    expect signature even if the general clause permits signature until end
                    1930.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
